#!/bin/sh
# The godot window: launch the Godot editor through `task godot:editor` (#17),
# which uses non-default LSP/DAP/remote-debug ports so it can run beside other
# Godot projects. Until that task exists, print how to start the editor.
#
# GODOT_EDITOR_ONCE=1 reports what it would run and exits, and DEV_REPO_ROOT
# overrides the repo root (tests use these).
set -eu

repo_root="${DEV_REPO_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd -P)}"
cd "${repo_root}"

tasks="$(task --list-all --json 2>/dev/null || true)"
defined="$(printf '%s\n' "${tasks}" | jq -r 'any(.tasks[]?; .name == "godot:editor")' 2>/dev/null || true)"
if [ "${defined}" != true ]; then
  cat <<'EOF'
godot: the Godot editor task is not here yet (issue #17).
Once #17 lands:
  task godot:editor   open the editor on godot/ (LSP 6305, DAP 6306, remote debug 6307)
EOF
  exit 0
fi

printf 'godot: task godot:editor\n'
if [ -n "${GODOT_EDITOR_ONCE:-}" ]; then exit 0; fi
exec task godot:editor
